# Oracle: VD dev-builtin-src (Sine: sinedc 0, ampl 1, freq 1k, tdphase 0, theta 0, delay 0) and
# runs: the phase parameter is `tdphase` (`phase` is the AC phase: run src-sine, VD's syntax line
# is wrong); `dc` is ignored, the op is the wave at t = 0 (DcRule::WaveAtZero: `dc=5` with
# sinedc=1 gives op 1); before `delay` the value at `delay`, tdphase included (op 3 with
# delay=0.25m tdphase=90: PreDelay::HoldDelayValue). `dc=0` on a wave type: a parameter the
# type does not read, dropped with the note P2203 (R42).
# codes: P2203
file "sine.sim" deck
  title "sine"
  model vsource source_v
  element vsource v1 (a 0) model=vsource wave=sin(offset=0 amplitude=1 freq=1k delay=0 damping=0 phase_deg=0 pre=hold_delay_value) dc_rule=wave_at_zero
  element vsource v2 (b 0) model=vsource ac_mag=1i ac_phase_deg=0 wave=sin(offset=1i amplitude=2i freq=10k delay=1u damping=1k phase_deg=90i pre=hold_delay_value) dc_rule=wave_at_zero
  element vsource v3 (c 0) model=vsource wave=sin(offset=0 amplitude=0.5 freq=1k delay=0 damping=0 phase_deg=0 pre=hold_delay_value) dc_rule=wave_at_zero
